# The Squiddy commit this graph is built against (AD-030-R17).
#
# WHY A FILE AND NOT A pyproject DEPENDENCY. Squiddy is a BUILD-TIME dependency of this graph, not
# a runtime dependency of the `seldon` package: `seldon/core/governed.py` reads a JSONL ledger and
# imports no Squiddy module, so a `pyproject.toml` entry would be a dependency Seldon never uses
# and would make Seldon un-installable wherever Squiddy is absent — which is every environment
# Seldon's own suite runs in. AD-030-R17 supersedes the `pyproject.toml` clause of AD-030-R10; the
# acyclicity and no-awareness clauses of R10 stand.
#
# WHY A COMMIT AND NOT A VERSION. The kit is one day old and its version number moves slower than
# its behaviour. The extraction this graph produces is a function of the parser, the assess
# criterion and the acquire adapter as they stood at a specific commit; a version range would make
# the corpus unreproducible without saying so.
#
# `make -C governed check-squiddy` verifies this, and every build target depends on it.
# To move the pin (DN-043 R-185, SQ-010): `squiddy governed repin <commit> --graph governed --layer
# references`, with the kit checked out at a commit that has a recorded full-suite pass. It re-gates
# every admitted document and re-admits only those whose gate output changed; no reset, no sweep.
#
# 0.3.0 (2026-09-12) is the kit release AD-030-R22 asked for: an admitted document whose file hash
# has moved is admissible again and costs that one document, so `make -C governed admit ID=<id>` is
# the edit path and `reset.sh` plus a sweep is the reset path. The ledger under this pin was cut by
# a full sweep, because the recipe itself moved in the same change (the `Name:` header field, the
# supersession pattern, the `Addendum NNN-X:` label) and every document's extraction moved with it.
#
# 0.3.1 keys an admission's evidence directory and its export by the content it admitted rather
# than by the day, which is what makes a SECOND admission of one document on one day actually run.
# Found by the first real re-ingest in this graph: the run reported thirteen stages passed and had
# re-extracted nothing, because make had every stage record from the morning's admission already.
#
# 0.3.2 makes the parse cache follow the source. Found the same way and worse: the next re-ingest
# DID run every stage and extracted the previous version of the document, because the intermediate
# was cached by document id alone. Every gate passed — the manifest and the ledger agreed about the
# hash, and nothing downstream compares the text.
#
# 0.3.3 carries `--reingest` through to the assess stage, which is the stage that decides. Forcing
# the write stage alone forced nothing: assess stopped the pipeline at `already_admitted` first.

# 0.8.0 at 4ac50a5 (SEL-001, 2026-10-02): the pin moves with the template's recipe change (the
# SEL-001 label forms, the front-anchored ruling label, the `ontology` DocKind) and the kit's
# node-unit index. One pin for all three governed graphs (Seldon, Squiddy, Arnold). From here the
# pin binds the kit's `squiddy/` tree, not the kit repository's HEAD (check_pin.py `kit_matches`).
# Re-ingested by reset and a full sweep, the reset path for a recipe change (AD-030-R22).

